{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "ADS-B / Mode S reception at 1090 MHz. Requires a bias-tee-powered L-band LNA (e.g. Nooelec SAWbird+ 1090) for reliable decoding — without one the link budget is marginal even overhead. bw_hz is 2 000 000: the adsb plugin's internal working rate is 2 MSPS, so matching the source rate avoids resample_poly overhead per chunk. Gain is set high (42 dB) since ADS-B bursts are very short (~120 µs) and the AGC in SDRTerm cannot react fast enough to per-burst amplitude changes.",
